From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH kbase-common 012] panvk: kbase-aware csif in device init

Purpose: Route the device-init scoreboard setup through
 panvk_get_csif_props() (kbase GLB interface on /dev/mali*). The direct
 panthor call reads garbage on a kbase device (zero register counts),
 corrupting scoreboard masks used by every later submit. Missed by the
 hunk filters (no 'kbase' string at the call site).
Source/Reference: https://github.com/wonderkast02/panvk-g720-kbase-csf
 branch android-candidate-beta-1.9.4
 (src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c).
Tested GPU: Poco X6 Pro / G615.
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21.
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f).
Dependencies: 006 (helper).
Validation test: Gate E compute with buffer access.

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
@@ -528,7 +528,7 @@

 #if PAN_ARCH >= 10
    const struct drm_panthor_csif_info *csif_info =
-      panthor_kmod_get_csif_props(device->kmod.dev);
+      panvk_get_csif_props(device);

    assert(csif_info->scoreboard_slot_count <= 16);
    device->csf.sb.count = csif_info->scoreboard_slot_count;
